{
  "id": 147318200,
  "iid": 6542,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "uds: Don't append parameter record if not available",
  "description": "I've recently worked with a CAN trace with UDS packets and noticed an assertion triggered by the UDS dissector. \n\nIf a UDS reply is decoded with `50 7e ff ff ff ff ff` meaning no parameter record is attached, the dissector will run into the following assert: \n\n```\n[Dissector bug, protocol UDS: C:\\gitlab-builds\\builds\\-fyeYoMP\\0\\wireshark\\wireshark\\epan\\tvbuff.c:4387: failed assertion \"len > 0\"]\n    [Expert Info (Error/Malformed): C:\\gitlab-builds\\builds\\-fyeYoMP\\0\\wireshark\\wireshark\\epan\\tvbuff.c:4387: failed assertion \"len > 0\"]\n        [C:\\gitlab-builds\\builds\\-fyeYoMP\\0\\wireshark\\wireshark\\epan\\tvbuff.c:4387: failed assertion \"len > 0\"]\n        [Severity level: Error]\n        [Group: Malformed]\n```\n\n![grafik](/uploads/610cc9fc71d9dd6b8d8c3a2bdea0b117/grafik.png)\n\nThe data hex dump:\n\n```\n0000   98 da fb ee 08 00 00 00 02 50 7e ff ff ff ff ff   .........P~.....\n```\n\nand the corresponding pcapng file: [uds-dissector-bug.pcapng](/uploads/5a5029ba415573e0331eb2898e168294/uds-dissector-bug.pcapng)\n\nThis is caused by calling `tvb_bytes_to_str_punct` with a length of `0`, which is `0` when the parameter record is missing. \n\nI've fixed the issue by checking the `parameter_record_length != 0` before calling `tvb_bytes_to_str_punkt`. \n\nFixed: \n\n```\nUnified Diagnostic Services\n    0.01 0000 = Service Identifier: Diagnostic Session Control (0x10)\n    .1.. .... = Reply Flag: 0x1\n    Diagnostic Session Control\n        Type: Unknown (0x7e)\n        Parameter Record: <MISSING>\n\n```\n\n![grafik](/uploads/5e88946bb1468265e9841e12a9527c08/grafik.png)\n\nI'm not sure if a missing parameter record is up to spec nor did I check if omitting the parameter record in this case is correct, but at least this will avoid running into the assertion failure. \n\nI'm open to suggestions if a better approch exists.",
  "state": "merged",
